  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, which substantially outperforms singleprofile RNA (0.485) and image-only (0.208). However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA), leaving the representation choice as a major unresolved variable. Question: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) directly tests whether a learned nonlinear representation (SCVI) outperforms linear PCA under the identical multiprofile+avgpool setting, isolating the encoder as the sole changed variable. Why this is best: It is the cleanest single-factor comparison against our current best, it reduces uncertainty about whether representation quality is a bottleneck before investing in multimodal fusion experiments, and the result will inform which RNA encoder to pair with image fusion in subsequent experiments. If SCVI matches or beats PCA, it reshapes the multimodal search space; if PCA is already near-optimal, we can confidently move to fusion testing."
